From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpine-riscv32 <alpine-riscv32@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:41:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: esp32s31: shrink the DMA pool and move it up

The coherent DMA pool takes 256 KiB of internal SRAM at 0x2f030000,
which is where the ESP-IDF Wi-Fi radio code needs its heap, buffers and
exception stack (0x2f030000-0x2f072380, plus 0x2f078c00-0x2f07cfb0).

Its users allocate a few pages: the EMAC rings (64 RX and 128 TX
descriptors of 32 bytes, one page each) and the dwc2 host status
buffer. Give it 20 KiB at 0x2f073000, the gap the radio layout leaves
for DMA descriptors. It stays in internal SRAM, which the data cache
does not cover, so the descriptors need no cache maintenance.
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts
index c0b39b790..fd01fec5c 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts
@@ -78,11 +78,17 @@ reserved-memory {
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges;
 
-		dma_pool: dma-pool@2f030000 {
+		/*
+		 * Coherent DMA memory for the EMAC rings and the USB host. It stays
+		 * in internal SRAM, which the data cache does not cover, and is kept
+		 * small so that 0x2f030000-0x2f072380 and 0x2f078c00-0x2f07cfb0 stay
+		 * free for the Wi-Fi radio code.
+		 */
+		dma_pool: dma-pool@2f073000 {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			linux,dma-default;
 			no-map;
-			reg = <0x2f030000 0x40000>;
+			reg = <0x2f073000 0x5000>;
 		};
 	};
 
